    "description": "7 Mile Pit Solar is a utility-scale solar project under development on a former mining site in Crawford County, Michigan. The project is intended to supply wholesale renewable electricity and follows an asset-heavy development model that depends on site control, permitting, interconnection, and a long-term offtake structure. Public materials describe the site as a repurposing of state land formerly used for sand and gravel extraction. Michigan's Department of Natural Resources awarded Circle Power a lease for the site in 2020, and Amber later partnered with Circle Power through the Circle Power Renewables platform. Reviewed public sources do not disclose the current project-level ownership percentages.",
